:: Heist Wren Approach
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Wren>><<person1>>

<<if $wrenTalkLocation is "pub">>
	You lean closer and tell Wren that Landry sent you about a job. <<He>> motions you towards a quiet corner of the pub, away from the other smugglers.
<<elseif $wrenTalkLocation is "gambling">>
	You lean closer and tell Wren that Landry sent you about a job. <<He>> looks away from the dice for the first time all evening, then tips <<his>> head towards the back of the room, where the noise of the table won't carry.
<<else>>
	You pull Wren away from the card table. One of <<his>> friends grumbles, but Wren lifts a hand without looking back. The complaint dies into a few sour looks.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">><<He>> looks you over, and <<his>> face softens. "Last time I saw you, you were in a more fragile state. You look well now."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">><<He>> tips <<his>> head, a sly grin tugging at <<his>> mouth. "I remember the catsuit. Bold choice. Very you."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">><<He>> raises an eyebrow. "Prison did not break you, then. Good. You'll need that kind of nerve for what I have in mind."
<<elseif $wrenSeen?.length>><<He>> studies you for a moment, then laughs. "Oh, wow. What's the hurry?"
<<else>><<He>> looks you over with interest. "So you're the one Landry keeps talking about."<</if>>
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	"I need your help," you say, speaking before you can lose your nerve. "It's about the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You glance aside, then make yourself meet <<his>> eyes. "Landry said you might help with something. The bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"Sorry to pull you away from your game," you say. "Landry sent me. It's about the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You give Wren a bright smile. "Sorry, darling, but this can't wait. Landry sent me, and it is about the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	"I was told to come to you," you say. "Landry thinks you can help with the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"Landry sent me," you say. "We've got a bank to rob, and I need to know if you're in."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Landry sent me," you say. "Try not to look too flattered. We need you for the bank."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"So... how do you feel about robbing a bank?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Landry sent me," you say. "We're planning something big. The bank."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren React]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren React
<<effects>>
Wren says nothing at first. Surprise crosses <<his>> face, then thought, then a sharp little smile. By the time <<he>> speaks, <<he>> looks fully interested.
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"Rob a bank," <<he>> repeats, grinning. "I wondered when someone would finally say that to my face."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"The bank." <<He>> gives a low whistle. "Straight to the point. I respect that."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"The bank," <<he>> says, as if enjoying the sound of it. "Very polite way to start a crime."
<<else>>
	"The bank. As in the only bank in this city. The one with connections that reach all the way up to..." 
	<<He>> trails off and whistles. "That bank."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> folds <<his>> arms and starts pacing. "Landry's been talking about that place for years. Never had anyone foolish enough to try it." <<He>> smiles. "That is a compliment, by the way."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren React 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren React 2
<<effects>>
<<He>> lifts one finger. "Before we go anywhere near the vault, we need information. Proper information. Not Landry's drunken stories."
<br><br>
<<if $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">>
	<<He>> smirks. "I've seen you move. You've got the instinct for this. Quick hands, quick head. But instinct alone gets people caught. We need careful watching."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">>
	"You got through prison. That tells me you can keep your head down, keep quiet, and notice things. That's exactly what I need from you."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">>
	<<He>> pauses. Something softer crosses <<his>> face, then disappears. "Last time we met, things were complicated. Fine. We'll leave it there. I still know you're tougher than you look, and I need that."
<<else>>
	<<He>> gives you a long, careful look. "I hope you're as good as Landry says you are."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Listen to Wren's plan|Heist Wren Plan]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Plan
<<effects>>
"Here's what you're going to do." Wren raises <<his>> hand and counts on <<his>> fingers. "You'll visit the bank as a customer. Make a deposit, make a withdrawal, ask a boring question at the counter. Anything normal."
<br><br>
<<He>> leans closer and lowers <<his>> voice.
<br><br>
"While you're there, you watch. Watch everything. Where the guards stand. Where the cameras point. Which doors need keycards, and which doors open if someone knows the right thing to say. When the tellers change places. How fast security reacts when something goes wrong. Every habit. Every pattern. Every small mistake."
<br><br>
<<He>> straightens and raises <<his>> hand again. "Seven visits. <span class="red">But do not go too often.</span> The guards are not stupid. Leave time between visits. If you feel anyone watching you, leave at once and come back another day... or another week."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Plan 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Plan 2
<<effects>>
<<He>> gives you a steady look. "If you make them too suspicious, they'll ban you from the bank. Then we have to start again, and I hate doing the same job twice."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	You swallow. "And if they catch me watching?"
	<br><br>
	"Then you'll wish they only banned you," <<he>> says plainly. The hard edge in <<his>> voice fades after a moment. "But you'll manage. Just act natural."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"And if they notice?" you ask, quieter than you meant to.
	<br><br>
	Wren's mouth twitches. "Then you leave before they make it a problem. You're there to watch them, not to be watched."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"So seven visits, with time between each one, and no hanging about," you say. "Understood."
	<br><br>
	"Exactly." <<He>> smiles, pleased. "See? Much easier when someone listens."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Seven visits to a bank," you say. "You do know how to show a person a thrilling evening."
	<br><br>
	"Save the show for the lobby," <<he>> says, amused. "Right now I need you to look forgettable."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You nod once. "Seven visits. Watch everything. Leave if it feels wrong."
	<br><br>
	"Good." <<He>> taps two fingers against <<his>> arm. "That kind of discipline keeps people alive."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"Seven visits. Spread out. No mistakes," you say.
	<br><br>
	"That's the spirit." <<He>> grins. "You make it sound almost professional."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Seven visits to the dullest building in town," you say. "You really know how to spoil a person."
	<br><br>
	"And yet here you are." <<He>> smiles back without missing a beat. "Go and be dull enough to blend in."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"Seven visits to the most boring building in the city," you say. "Thrilling."
	<br><br>
	"Says the person who agreed to rob it." <<He>> grins. "Now go be boring. Boring, but observant."
<<else>>
	You nod. "Seven visits. Spread them out. Don't get noticed."
	<br><br>
	"Quick study. I like that." <<He>> smiles.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.wrenRecruited to true>>
<<if $wrenTalkLocation is "pub">>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to Wren|Smuggler Pub Wren]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $wrenTalkLocation is "gambling">>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to Wren|Pub Gambling Wren]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Estate]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Bank Observation
<<effects>><<bankHeistObservation>>
<<set _heist to $xchange.bankHeist>><<set _obs to _heist.observationDays>>
<<if setup.hbsc.isBanned()>>
	<<set _banDays to setup.hbsc.getBanRemainingDays()>>
	You step inside the bank, but a guard comes over before you can settle in. 
	"We've seen you looking where you shouldn't. Management would like you to stay away for a while. For your own comfort."
	<br><br>
	You are led back out to the street before you can even answer.
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You've been banned from the bank for <<print _banDays>> more day<<if _banDays isnot 1>>s<</if>></span>. Your observation progress has been reset.
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif _heistVisitType is "sameDay">>
	You walk into the bank again, then quickly realise there is nothing new to learn today. The same guards are in the same places. The same tellers are behind the counters. The same cameras watch from above.
	<br><br>
	<<if playerHasXChangeBody() and !$daily.xchangeBankSuspicionReduced and $xchange_fame lt 400>>
		<<set $daily.xchangeBankSuspicionReduced to true>>
		<<if $xchange_fame lt 100>>
			<<set _heist.suspicion to Math.max(0, _heist.suspicion - 3)>>
			<span class="gold">The staff barely recognise you.</span> Your X-Change look does not match the description they were given.
		<<elseif $xchange_fame lt 250>>
			<<set _heist.suspicion to Math.max(0, _heist.suspicion - 2)>>
			<span class="green">A few staff glance at you, then look away.</span> Your X-Change look makes them unsure.
		<<else>>
			<<set _heist.suspicion to Math.max(0, _heist.suspicion - 1)>>
			<span class="teal">The staff seem suspicious, but can't prove anything.</span> Your X-Change look gives them doubt.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if _heist.suspicion gte 5 and _heist.suspicion lt 8>>
		<<if _heist.suspicion gte 7>>
			But a guard near the entrance is already watching you. <span class="red">You need to stay away for a while.</span>
		<<else>>
			But one of the guards looks your way more than once. <span class="pink">You may be drawing attention.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif _heistVisitType is "consecutive">>
	You join the queue and try to look like any other customer. But you were here yesterday, and the place feels too familiar. The tellers are the same. The guards are the same.
	<br><br>
	<<if playerHasXChangeBody() and !$daily.xchangeBankSuspicionReduced and $xchange_fame lt 400>>
		<<set $daily.xchangeBankSuspicionReduced to true>>
		<<if $xchange_fame lt 100>>
			<<set _heist.suspicion to Math.max(0, _heist.suspicion - 3)>>
			<span class="gold">The staff barely recognise you.</span> Your X-Change look does not match the description they were given.
		<<elseif $xchange_fame lt 250>>
			<<set _heist.suspicion to Math.max(0, _heist.suspicion - 2)>>
			<span class="green">A few staff glance at you, then look away.</span> Your X-Change look makes them unsure.
		<<else>>
			<<set _heist.suspicion to Math.max(0, _heist.suspicion - 1)>>
			<span class="teal">The staff seem suspicious, but can't prove anything.</span> Your X-Change look gives them doubt.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<<if _heist.suspicion gte 5 and _heist.suspicion lt 8>>
		<<if _heist.suspicion gte 7>>
			But a guard near the entrance watches you with a hard stare. <span class="red">You're drawing a lot of attention.</span>
		<<else>>
			But you catch a guard looking your way more than once. <span class="pink">You may be drawing attention.</span>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	Wren's warning comes back to you. Back-to-back days will get you noticed.
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	/* Valid observation, spaced properly */
	You step into the bank and take your place in the queue. Marble shines under the lights. Polished brass catches your eye. You keep your face blank and your body relaxed, while your eyes keep moving.
	<<if _heist.suspicion gte 5 and _heist.suspicion lt 8>>
		<<if _heist.suspicion gte 7>>
			But a guard near the entrance keeps looking back at you. <span class="red">You're drawing a lot of attention</span>. You should leave more time between visits.
		<<elseif _heist.suspicion gte 5>>
			You notice a guard glance your way more than once. <span class="pink">You may be drawing attention</span>. Try leaving more time between visits.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if _obs is 1>>
		Your first visit gives you the basic layout. Two cameras cover the public floor, one above the entrance and one aimed at the teller windows. Three armed guards watch the room. Behind the counter is a service door with a keycard reader beside it.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 1/7: Floor layout noted.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 2>>
		On your second visit, you come at a different time and watch the guards instead of the counters. One stays by the entrance, one walks across the lobby, and one stands near a small desk at the back. The walking guard passes the service door about every four minutes.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 2/7: Guard rotation pattern identified.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 3>>
		On your third visit, you spot a weak point in the camera view. A pillar near the eastern wall blocks part of the angle. The service door opens twice while you wait, and you glimpse stairs leading down.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 3/7: Camera blind spot and basement access located.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 4>>
		On your fourth visit, a man in an expensive suit arrives. A guard lets <<him>> through the service door after a short exchange. It must be some kind of spoken code.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 4/7: VIP access procedure observed.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 5>>
		On your fifth visit, you time the shift change. At one-thirty, the walking guard is replaced. For about thirty seconds, both guards disappear into the break room corridor.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 5/7: Shift change window identified.</span>
	<<elseif _obs is 6>>
		On your sixth visit, you look more closely at the service door lock. It uses an old magnetic strip reader, the kind Wren could probably bypass in <<nnpc_his "Wren">> sleep. You also spot a maintenance hatch near the toilets. It likely opens into the building's utility corridor.
		<br><br>
		<span class="teal">Observation 6/7: Lock type and alternate access route catalogued.</span>
	<<elseif _obs gte 7>>
		On your seventh visit, you check every detail again. Guard positions. Camera coverage. The shift change. The magnetic lock. The maintenance hatch. The stairs down towards the vault.
		<br><br>
		You have everything you need.
		<br><br>
		<span class="gold">Observation complete. Report back to Wren.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|High Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Heist Wren Report Observation
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Wren>><<person1>>
<<if $wrenTalkLocation is "pub">>
	You join Wren in a quiet corner of the pub and tell <<him>> that you finished watching the bank.
<<elseif $wrenTalkLocation is "gambling">>
	Wren pushes <<his>> chair back from the dice table and walks you to the quiet end of the room. You tell <<him>> that you finished watching the bank.
<<else>>
	You pull Wren aside again. By now <<his>> friends seem almost used to it, though a few still send dirty looks your way.
<</if>>
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> what you saw: the floor plan, the guard routes, the camera blind spot, the shift change, the magnetic locks, and the maintenance hatch.
<br><br>
Wren listens without interrupting. <<His>> head tilts slightly, and <<his>> eyes stay fixed on you. When you finish, <<he>> is quiet for a moment. Then <<he>> grins. "You're good at this. Better than I expected."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Report Observation 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Observation 2
<<effects>>
Wren starts pacing. <<He>> gets faster as the plan comes together in <<his>> head.
<br><br>
"The maintenance hatch is our way in. It should connect to the utility corridor. That corridor should run near the vault stairs. I can handle the magnetic locks. Those old strip readers have a weakness."
<br><br>
<<He>> stops and turns back to you. "The shift change gives us our best thirty seconds. That's when we move from the utility corridor to the stairs.
After that, it gets harder. The vault level has its own power and its own security."
<<if $skulduggery gte 950>><<He>> smiles. "With your skills, I like our chances."
<<elseif $skulduggery gte 650>><<He>> tilts <<his>> head. "It will be close, but we can do it."
<<else>><<His>> expression grows more serious. "It's going to be dangerous. Make sure you're ready."<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Report Observation 3]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Observation 3
<<effects>>
Wren folds <<his>> arms and leans back against the wall.
<br><br>
"I can handle the locks, the doors, and getting us in and out. But the vault's electronic security?" <<He>> shakes <<his>> head. "That's not my skill. <span class="teal">We need our friend at the pub</span> to look over your notes. They can work out the electronic layout and tell us how to avoid it."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	"You mean M-Mickey?" you ask quietly.
	<br><br>
	"Don't say their name out loud," <<he>> says, though <<hes>> smiling. "But yes. Bring your notes to the pub. Landry can pass them on."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"The one at the pub?" you ask, lowering your voice without thinking.
	<br><br>
	"That's the one." <<He>> smiles faintly. "See? You do know how to be discreet."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"To the pub, then," you say. "I'll make sure it gets to them."
	<br><br>
	"Good." <<He>> nods. "The sooner they see it, the sooner we can move."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"So I carry secrets to the pub and pretend I'm not enjoying myself," you say.
	<br><br>
	"Yes," <<he>> says. "Try especially hard on the pretending part."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You nod. "I'll take it to them."
	<br><br>
	"Good." <<He>> pushes off the wall. "Simple jobs are the ones people ruin by thinking too much."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"The pub. Fine. I'll get it done," you say.
	<br><br>
	"That's what I like to hear." <<He>> grins. "Quick and clean."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"So I get to play courier again," you say. "How glamorous."
	<br><br>
	"Call it a vital part of the job," <<he>> says. "Though I know you prefer work with an audience."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"So I get to play courier again," you sneer. "Wonderful."
	<br><br>
	"Think of it as networking." <<He>> grins. "Now go. The sooner they see these notes, the sooner we move."
<<else>>
	You nod. "The pub. I'll get it to them."
	<br><br>
	"Good. The sooner they see this, the sooner we move."
<</if>>
<br><br><<set $xchange.bankHeist.wrenReported to true>>
<<set $xchange.bankHeist.suspicion to null>><<set $xchange.bankHeist.lastObservationDay to null>>
<<link [[Are you nervous?|Heist Wren Report Nervous]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Nervous
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
	"A-Are you nervous?" you ask quietly.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You hesitate, then ask, "You're nervous too, aren't you?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite")>>
	"May I ask something?" you say. "Are you nervous about this?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Tell me honestly," you say. "Are you nervous, or are you just building suspense?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
	"You look calm enough," you say. "But are you nervous?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
	"What, you're not even a little scared?" you ask.
<<else>>
	"Are you nervous about this?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
Wren's expression goes still. For a moment, <<he>> looks more honest than usual.
<br><br>
<<if $wrenSeenLast is "catsuit">>
	"I've broken into a lot of places. Worn a lot of disguises." <<He>> smiles faintly. "But nothing like this. This one matters."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "prison">>
	"I've been locked up before. I know what it feels like. And I know what kind of place this bank is." <<He>> meets your eyes. "So yes. A little."
<<elseif $wrenSeenLast is "pregnancy">>
	"I've seen enough to know things don't always go to plan." <<His>> face is hard to read. "But we go anyway. That's the job."
<<else>>
	"Nervous? No. Nervous is for people who have something to lose. I'm..." <<He>> searches for the word. "Alert."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Heist Wren Report Nervous 2]]>><</link>>

:: Heist Wren Report Nervous 2
<<effects>>
Wren straightens. The honest moment is gone as quickly as it came. "See you on the other side."
<br><br>
<<if $wrenTalkLocation is "pub">>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to Wren|Smuggler Pub Wren]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $wrenTalkLocation is "gambling">>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to Wren|Pub Gambling Wren]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Estate]]>><<unset $wrenTalkLocation>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
